hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1553","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Khurami, narrated to us Yahya bin Adam, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, on the authority of his father, said: I came to Medina and met Ubayy ibn Ka’b. Muhammad bin Muammar told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Basir, on the authority of His father, he said: We returned Ubayy ibn Ka’b. So he mentioned the hadith on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: “The front row is like the row of angels, and if only you knew its virtue.” \You would have hastened to do so\"""""
